tunately i would say that dhs has  already decided  to put further restrictions on who ice  law enforcement officers can and cannot  deport  so even though the court ruling is a win  dhs has already given ice instructions  that they can only remove individuals in  three specific classes  those that come across the border those  that are aggravated felons and those  that are  essentially terrorists and which is very  concerning that takes  off the board about 80 to maybe 90  percent of individuals they could  legally remove out of the country and so  again just more concerning actions from  the biden administration  chad the administration also halted the  border wall construction  leaving high volume areas like the rio  grande valley  quite vulnerable we have a shot of the  map here to show people where  most of the people are coming in i know  that your colleagues  have said it's 4 000 people at the  border every day  what is the situation that the the  border patrol agent's face on the ground  walk us through this here yeah  absolutely the border wall system and  i've talked about it  numerous times it's not only that  physical infrastructure which people  usually assume that fence  but it's the it's the lights it's the  cameras it's the roads it's the fiber  optic sensors  that gives border patrol agents the full  picture there on the border and so you  mentioned rgv  there in texas that is ground zero for  illegal entries  into the united states and we had  designated certain high priority  areas for a border wall system and now  we know that the bike administration has  stopped all construction so  it puts a further strain on the men and  women of the border patrol to do their  job and at the end of the day  what it means is you're going to see  more and more individuals coming across  those  areas you mentioned about thirty five  hundred to four thousand  a day is who border patrol is picking up  that doesn't account for what we call  the got aways which is an